                'en' => 'A rock of about 15 m3, weighing around 36 tonnes, broke away from the cliff, covered the 130 m of slope down to the track in about ten seconds at about 70 km/h, and went through two lines of protective screens. It hit the panoramic saloon of the leading car, then bounced over the train and came to rest near national road 202.',
